# MONTH9 — 90s Nostalgia (fact-checked Nov 2026)

FACT_OR_FAKE=[("The first text message ever sent said 'Merry Christmas'.", True, "Neil Papworth sent 'Merry Christmas' to Vodafone director Richard Jarvis on 3 December 1992."),
 ('Tamagotchis were invented in Japan in the 1990s.', True, 'Bandai released the Tamagotchi in Japan in 1996, creating a global virtual pet craze.'),
 ("Simba's father in The Lion King is named Scar.", False, "Simba's father is Mufasa. Scar is his scheming uncle."),
 ('The Spice Girls are the best-selling female group of all time.', True, 'Formed in the 90s, they have sold over 85 million records worldwide — more than any other girl group.'),
 ('The first Harry Potter book was rejected by 12 publishers before being accepted.',
  True,
  "J.K. Rowling faced multiple rejections before Bloomsbury published Harry Potter and the Philosopher's Stone in 1997."),
 ('The PlayStation 1 was originally designed as a CD-ROM add-on for the Super Nintendo.',
  True,
  'Sony developed it in partnership with Nintendo before the deal fell through, leading to the standalone PlayStation.'),
 ("Friends was almost called 'Insomnia Cafe'.", True, "Early working titles for Friends included 'Insomnia Cafe' and 'Friends Like Us'."),
 ('The World Wide Web was invented by Tim Berners-Lee.', True, 'He proposed it at CERN in 1989 and the Web went public in 1991.'),
 ('Nirvana took its band name from a Buddhist idea.', True, 'Kurt Cobain said he wanted a pretty name; in Buddhism, nirvana means freedom from suffering.'),
 ('Michael Jordan starred alongside Bugs Bunny in Space Jam.', True, 'The 1996 film mixed live action with Looney Tunes animation.'),
 ('The first Google search engine was launched from a garage in 1998.', True, 'Larry Page and Sergey Brin launched Google in 1998, initially working out of a garage in Menlo Park.'),
 ('Furby was originally designed for the Japanese market.', False, 'Furby was an American creation by Tiger Electronics, first released in 1998 and then sold worldwide.'),
 ('The Hubble Space Telescope was launched in the 1990s.', True, 'Hubble was launched on April 24, 1990, aboard the Space Shuttle Discovery.'),
 ('Windows 95 sold more than a million copies in its first week.', True, 'It sold around 7 million copies in the first five weeks — a record-breaking launch for software at the time.'),
 ('The Mighty Morphin Power Rangers were originally a Japanese show.', True, "They were adapted from the Japanese 'Super Sentai' series, with new footage of American actors spliced in."),
 ('Titanic (1997) was the first film to earn $1 billion at the global box office.', True, 'It became the highest-grossing film of all time at that point, earning over $1.8 billion globally.'),
 ('The yo-yo was originally a weapon before it became a toy.', False, 'Despite the popular story, there is no credible historical evidence that yo-yos were used as weapons.'),
 ('Slap bracelets were banned in some US schools in the early 1990s.', True, 'Multiple schools banned them after reports of children getting cuts from the exposed metal inside worn bracelets.'),
 ('DVDs first went on sale in the 1990s.', True, 'DVD players launched in Japan in 1996 and in the United States in 1997.'),
 ("The hit version of 'Macarena' was a remix.", True, 'Los del Río released it in 1993; the 1995 Bayside Boys remix became the worldwide smash.'),
 ('Beanie Babies were so popular in the 90s that people invested millions in them expecting them to gain value.',
  True,
  'The beanie baby craze led people to buy, collect, and store them in protective cases, expecting huge returns — most were ultimately worth very little.'),
 ('The Goosebumps book series was created by R.L. Stine in the 1990s.', True, 'R.L. Stine launched the Goosebumps series in 1992, and it became one of the best-selling book series of all time.'),
 ('Bill Nye the Science Guy first aired on TV in 1993.', True, 'Bill Nye the Science Guy premiered on September 10, 1993 on KCTS in Seattle.'),
 ('The Backstreet Boys were put together through an open audition in New York.', False, 'They were formed in Orlando, Florida in 1993 through connections made by businessman Lou Pearlman.'),
 ("Pokémon was originally called 'Capsule Monsters'.",
  True,
  "Creator Satoshi Tajiri originally proposed the concept under the working title 'Capsule Monsters' before it became Pocket Monsters/Pokémon."),
 ('Keanu Reeves turned down the role of Neo in The Matrix.', False, 'Reeves took the role. Will Smith is the one who famously turned it down.'),
 ('The original Game Boy had a color screen.', False, "The original Game Boy, released in 1989, had a distinctive yellow-green monochrome screen. The Game Boy Color didn't arrive until 1998."),
 ('AOL Instant Messenger launched in the 1990s.', True, 'AIM launched in 1997 and became one of the dominant ways people communicated online through the late 90s and 2000s.'),
 ('Mike Myers was not the first actor cast as Shrek.', True, "Chris Farley recorded most of Shrek's lines before his death in 1997."),
 ("Will Smith's character in The Fresh Prince was also named Will Smith.", True, 'The show used his real name for the character, a fictionalised version of himself.')]

